Only two of the reference's 19 fuzz targets carry a checked-in seed corpus.
Everything else is generated at run time by go-fuzz-headers, so there is no
file to copy — see ../SEEDS.md for the per-target detail.

  FuzzDistillPolicy/  27 files
    Reference path : pkg/policy/testdata/fuzz/FuzzDistillPolicy
    Target         : pkg/policy/simulate_fuzz_test.go FuzzDistillPolicy
    Shape          : Go `testing.F` corpus format — a "go test fuzz v1" header
                     line followed by one `[]byte("...")` literal. The byte
                     string is consumed by makeFuzzEntries() as a packed
                     sequence of policy-rule descriptors (direction, default
                     deny, selector, port range, protocol, deny flag), so each
                     file is a regression-captured *rule set* that once made
                     the compiled map state and the reference simulator
                     disagree.
    Value          : these are crash/differential regressions, i.e. the exact
                     rule combinations where deny precedence, wildcard
                     shadowing or port-range merging went wrong once already.
                     They are the highest-value 27 files in the whole harvest.

  FuzzUint8/  3 files
    Reference path : pkg/container/bitlpm/testdata/fuzz/FuzzUint8
    Target         : pkg/container/bitlpm/fuzz_test.go FuzzUint8
    Shape          : same "go test fuzz v1" + `[]byte("...")` format. The bytes
                     are read as (value, prefix-length) pairs and inserted into
                     a uint8 LPM trie; the invariants checked are Len(),
                     Ancestors() returning the longest-prefix entry, and Len()
                     decrementing correctly on Delete().
    Value          : LPM trie edge cases (prefix 0, duplicate prefixes after
                     masking, delete of an interior node).

Format conversion
-----------------
The Go corpus format is not cargo-fuzz's. A converter lives at
tools/fuzz-corpus-convert (to be written): it strips the "go test fuzz v1"
line, unquotes the Go byte-string literal, and writes the raw bytes as one
file per seed into fuzz/corpus/<target>/. Keep the originals here verbatim so
a re-harvest at a newer reference tag stays a diff.

Modifications
-------------
None. All 30 files are byte-identical to the reference.
